.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt EGGHEAD-AGENTS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm egghead-agents
.Nd manage agents and their capabilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm egghead agents
.Op Cm list
.Nm egghead agents
.Cm new
.Op Fl -name Ar name
.Op Fl -model Ar model
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Nm egghead agents
.Cm grant Ar agent-id Op Ar spec
.Op Fl -yes
.Nm egghead agents
.Cm revoke Ar agent-id Ar spec
.Nm egghead agents
.Cm capabilities Ar agent-id
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An agent is a record with
.Cm class: agent .
The body is the system prompt; the frontmatter declares the model,
the tags, and the capabilities the agent holds. Drop a record with
that class into the records directory and an agent process starts.
Edit it and the process hot-reloads. Delete it and the process stops.
There is no separate registration step.
.Pp
.Cm agents
operates on the agents currently running in the supervision tree.
.Cm grant
and
.Cm revoke
both rewrite the agent's record on disk; the running process restarts
with the new authority.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "capabilities id"
.It Cm list
Print the running roster: name, id, and model. Default when no
subcommand is given.
.It Cm new
Create a new agent interactively. The wizard picks an id, a model,
a starting capability bundle, and writes the file. Use the flags
below to skip individual prompts.
.It Cm grant Ar agent-id Op Ar spec
Add a capability to an agent. With no
.Ar spec ,
opens an interactive picker over the catalog, sorted from low risk
to high. With a
.Ar spec ,
applies it directly after a confirmation; pass
.Fl -yes
to skip the prompt. The grant is written into the agent's record.
.It Cm revoke Ar agent-id Ar spec
Remove a capability from the agent's record.
.It Cm capabilities Ar agent-id
Print the agent's currently held capabilities, sorted by risk tier.
Aliased as
.Cm caps .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--model model"
.It Fl -name Ar name
Agent id, for
.Cm new .
Skips the name prompt.
.It Fl -model Ar model
Model in
.Sy provider/model
form, for
.Cm new .
Skips the picker.
.It Fl -dry-run
Preview the agent record without writing it, for
.Cm new .
.It Fl y , Fl -yes
Skip the confirmation prompt, for
.Cm grant .
.It Fl -config Ar path
Override the configuration file location.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help.
.El
.Sh CAPABILITY SPEC GRAMMAR
The compact spec form mirrors the YAML grammar described in
.Xr egghead 7
and the
.Sx Capabilities
guide:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
records.read
records.update{classes=[deliberation,inbox]}
net.get{hosts=[*.github.com,api.anthropic.com]}
proc.exec{in=~/Work,cmds=[rg,jq]}
.Ed
.Pp
Internal verbs
.Pq Sy records.* , Sy agent.*
default to the universe in their bare form. External verbs
.Pq Sy net.* , Sy fs.* , Sy proc.*
default to empty in their bare form: a typo or omitted scope cannot
silently grant unrestricted external access. Wide grants are
permitted; they have to be written down explicitly.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create an agent interactively:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead agents new
.Ed
.Pp
Create one without prompts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead agents new --name scout --model anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect and adjust held capabilities:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead agents capabilities scout
egghead agents grant scout 'net.get{hosts=[*.github.com]}'
egghead agents revoke scout records.update
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr egghead-llm 1 ,
.Xr egghead-skills 1 ,
.Xr egghead-tools 1 ,
.Xr egghead-doctor 1 ,
.Xr egghead 1 ,
.Xr egghead 7
